do  well following the guidelines that i put  in the video  what's most important that you do is  make sure that you  sign the return envelope on the outside  of that return envelope that's the  signature that we use  to make sure that your identity matches  what we have in the system  so that's the number one thing that you  need to make sure and do  then you need to make sure and get that  ballot turned into us before the  deadline  whether you're dropping it in the post  office mailbox  or delivering it to a mail ballot drop  off the deadline to have that dropped  off with the drop off or  in the post office postmarked is  november 3rd  we can accept any mail that comes in all  the way through  november 10th to make sure that we're  giving plenty of opportunity for that  postmark ballot to get in and if you  make it  to a mail ballot drop off as long as  it's deposited  by election day november 3rd we'll get  it processed and counted  are we able to track our mail ballot to  make sure it reached out reached you on  time  yes either using the secretary of  state's website or my website you can  log  into registered voter services at our  website  and check the status of your ballot it  takes time for us to process that ballot  and get it scanned into the system  to show what the status of that ballot  is  once we've received it so once you mail  it you need to give three or four days  at a minimum before you can check the  status  and see how we've received it and  whether it's being processed to be  counted  when will we know who won the election  unofficial results will be released on  election night  and that will represent the in-person  voting that took place during early  voting  and on election day minus the  provisional ballots  a mail ballots will continue to be  counted well after election day because  we have to process  all of the mail ballot drop-offs and  anything that comes through the mail  until after the election so the official  report will be  sent to the county commission for canvas  on november 16th  so that's when the official results will  be available for all to see  when will the mail ballots be counted  again as a result of ab4 they've  increased the amount of time that we  have here in clark county to count those  ballots  so 15 days prior to election day we will  begin to tabulate ballots  but not release counts on on results  we will have the number of people who  have voted  by mail however we won't release any  totals until  election night when we've received  confirmation from the secretary of  state's office that all 17 counties have  finished voting  after election night um we will continue  to release periodic results as far as  the status  on the counts related to what is being  counted on a daily basis that first  report will be available uh the thursday  after election day which would be  november 5th  how's the training and staffing coming  along for the election workers  we've received a tremendous response  from the general public  and we're very happy to report that it  looks like we'll be able to find enough  workers for both the early voting and  election day process  however we are definitely in need of  people who  can translate in spanish and filipino  which we're federally required to  support and  also we're looking to set up a special  hotline although we're not  mandated to do so we're going to  proactively work to try to provide  support  for those native languages in vietnamese  korean  and mandarin so if you have any of those  abilities to translate and you're  willing to work please contact our  office  and let us know that you're willing to  support and work the polls  will there be information about election  observers available  basically for any part of the process  anybody who wants to observe the  election either early voting or election  day  they simply need to check in with the  team leader at any of those sites  they'll have to sign some documentation  and of course follow the rules we'll  have a designated location  in all of our polling places where those  observers can watch  they cannot disrupt the polling place  while they're observing  and they cannot interact with voters  while they're in the process of signing  in  and casting their ballot if you need  additional information  feel free to call our office at  voters from 702-4555 19. we've had  tremendous support from the county  and our mac department that is providing  ppe to all departments  we are very happy to report there is no  shortage of supplies  and we are prepared to provide face  masks  face shields plenty of disinfectant  and plenty of signage to make sure that  we keep  people socially distanced as they're  waiting in line  and also to disinfect all hard surfaces  at all of the polling places  so peace feel comfortable that if you do  choose to vote in person  that they will be a safe polling place  however i will encourage you  if you're at all concerned about being  in large groups as a result of the  pandemic  this is the main reason why we've  provided you with a mail-in ballot take  advantage of that mail-in ballot and  send it back to us  when will i receive my mail ballot the  out-of-state are actually the overseas  ballots are going to be going out this  weekend  we meet met the deadline requirement and  out-of-state ballots will begin going  out the following week  all of the local ballots will begin  dropping into the mail on october 7th  so after that point i would  give it at least five or six days and if  you have not received your ballot and  you know you should have received one  you need to begin to contact our office  contact our office directly so that we  can make arrangements to either send you  a new ballot  or send one electronically to you so  that you can vote and get it back to us  to cast your ballot  i want to thank you for joining us  tonight at our town hall i hope that i  provided some valuable information  related to the election and giving you  the options that you can take advantage  of whether you're voting by mail or  whether you're voting in person during  early voting or on election day  as always information about the coming  election is also available on our  website which is www.clarkcountynv.gov  forward slash vote or you can always  call my office at 702-455-vote  please exercise your right to vote don't  lose your voice in the community come  out and vote  you
 

